state-vector introspection, distributed tensor sharding, and hardware-accelerated
zk-SNARK pipelines.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}

MLB--MACSE v4.0 extends the v3.0 architecture by incorporating autonomous
inference loops, hardware-accelerated cryptographic modules, and distributed
tensor evolution. The system fuses MLB Statcast telemetry with astrophysical
entropy streams---including CMB anisotropy fields and gravitational wave strain
data---to construct universe-mimetic stochastic boundaries for baseball physics
simulation. The v4.0 release introduces a full hardware--software co-design
framework enabling real-time inference, secure analytics, and multi-stadium
simulation.

